{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Rivian went from no revenue in FY2020 to $5,387 million in FY2025, a 48.1% three-year CAGR from FY2022 [F2][F7][D342]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The step change came in FY2022, when revenue jumped 2914.5% to $1,658 million as deliveries began [F4][D83]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "That ramp was driven by increased deliveries of 19,412 vehicles [P67]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Growth then decelerated sharply to 12.1% in FY2024 and 8.4% in FY2025 [D187][D239]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2025 automotive revenue fell on 9,332 fewer deliveries, partly from expiration of 45W tax credits [P22]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Software and services contributed 21.6pp of FY2025's 8.4% growth, while new electric vehicles subtracted 10.5pp [D295][D288][D239]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Software and services revenue rose 221.7% on vehicle electrical architecture and software development services for the Joint Venture [D294][P18]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Software and services reached 28.9% of revenue in FY2025 versus 9.7% in FY2024 [D293][D290]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating expenses grew 6.9% against revenue growth of 8.4%, so incremental operating margin was 264.7% [D258][D239][D265]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted shares rose 17.1% in FY2025, so EPS improved 34.5% while net loss shrank 23.2% [D260][D242][D241]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin of -66.5% in FY2025 is the window high but still far below the -129.4% median [F31][D325][D326]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin turned positive at 2.7%, up 26.8pp, versus a -45.8% window median [F19][D252][D332]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The gross-margin gain came from higher average selling prices and lower cost per vehicle [P20]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Cost of revenue fell 15.0% on fewer vehicles produced and lower raw material and conversion costs [D255][P21]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "SG&A was the one drag, costing 0.5pp as it grew 9.9% on go-to-market expansion [D269][D257]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of -$779 million was -14.5% of revenue, and free cash flow of -$2,489 million was -46.2% [F64][D227][F78][D226]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The operating cash improvement was primarily driven by a significant reduction in net loss [P4]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex rose 49.9% to $1,710 million, or 31.7% of revenue and 2.18x D&A [D246][F71][D225][D228]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The capex increase funded expansion of production capacity at the Normal Factory [P3]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash fell to $1,642 million in FY2025 from $3,259 million, with total debt flat at $4,440 million [D231][D179][D230]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The current ratio dropped to 2.33x, the window low, from a 4.94x median [F129][D339][D341]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Financing inflow of $886 million came mainly from $750 million of Class A shares issued to Volkswagen Group [F92][P2]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted shares rose 17.1% in FY2025, and equity fell 30.0% to $4,594 million [D260][D249][F142]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Rivian has posted a net loss in each of the last seven years, from -$426 million in FY2019 to -$3,646 million in FY2025 [R1][F32][F38]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Stock-based compensation was 13.8% of revenue in FY2025 and at least 10% in each of the last five years [R2][D223]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Cash and investments of $6,082 million cover only 2.4 years of the latest burn [D229][D236]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "New electric vehicles were 67.6% of revenue and fell 12.5% in FY2025 [D286][D287]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Product revenue members sum to 129% of consolidated revenue, so they cannot be added [R6]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin: a print above the FY2025 level of 2.7% would confirm the cost trend, while a return below zero would reverse it [F19]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow: a move above the FY2025 -$779 million toward breakeven would confirm the burn trend [F64]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Software and services share: holding above the FY2025 28.9% would sustain the mix shift [D293]."}
  ]}
]}
